    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d161">

                <pb facs="0136" n="127" xml:id="pg127"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/882a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Heath</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-12">June 12, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1590. Please repeat following to Legations, Stockholm, Oslo, Copenhagen, The
                    Hague and Brussels.</p>
                <p>Americans in Europe have been continually warned from the outbreak of hostilities
                    to depart for the United States while they could obtain transportation.
                    Practically all means of transportation to the United States for them have now
                    been cut off by Italy’s entry into the war. The Department therefore will not
                    further authorize loans from its limited funds for repatriation expenses pending
                    further developments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
